WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.607 --> 00:00:16.110
then on, the king of Lilliput did not demand much of me.

2
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.912
I suppose that was because he no longer liked me.

3
00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.636
I could do as I pleased and go wherever I liked in Lilliput.

4
00:00:25.996 --> 00:00:32.641
Not long after the Blefuscan officials visited me, I had an opportunity to help the king of Lilliput.

5
00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:38.605
About midnight one night, people screaming outside my house woke me up.

6
00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:43.508
They were frantic, and I could not understand what they were shouting.

7
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:46.870
Suddenly, some palace officials arrived.

8
00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:49.832
"Hurry!" one of them cried.

9
00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:51.794
"You must come with us.

10
00:00:52.254 --> 00:00:54.876
It's an emergency—the palace is on fire!"

11
00:00:54.896 --> 00:00:59.439
"Of course," I replied and rushed to get dressed.

12
00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.588
"Jump onto my hand.

13
00:01:01.608 --> 00:01:03.910
I'll carry you all so that we'll get there quickly."

14
00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.012
We hurried to the palace.

15
00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:11.176
The fire had started by accident in the room of one of the queen's maids.

16
00:01:11.977 --> 00:01:15.840
A burning candle had fallen over and some curtains caught on fire.

17
00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.764
When we arrived, the fire was out of control.

18
00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:22.986
Many people were trying to put it out.

19
00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:29.412
Two ladders were leaning up against the castle walls near the open windows of the maid's room.

20
00:01:30.264 --> 00:01:32.225
A man was at the top of each ladder.

21
00:01:32.985 --> 00:01:35.846
People were passing buckets of water up to those men.

22
00:01:36.746 --> 00:01:40.327
The men threw water on the flames, but it did not do much good.

23
00:01:40.927 --> 00:01:44.628
The Lilliputian buckets were tiny and held very little water.

24
00:01:45.528 --> 00:01:48.789
As each minute passed, the fire burned more strongly.

25
00:01:48.809 --> 00:01:52.010
"The fire's spread to another room!"

26
00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.371
cried one of the men on the ladder.

27
00:01:54.391 --> 00:01:57.091
"The whole palace might burn down!"

28
00:01:57.832 --> 00:01:58.832
shouted the other one.

29
00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:02.733
A feeling in my body suddenly gave me an idea.

30
00:02:03.673 --> 00:02:06.874
The night before, I had drunk quite a lot of wine.

31
00:02:07.474 --> 00:02:09.455
The wine had made me very thirsty.

32
00:02:10.355 --> 00:02:15.756
So I had drunk a lot of water too, enough to fill about twenty Lilliputian barrels.

33
00:02:16.677 --> 00:02:21.558
I had felt so tired after drinking the wine that I had fallen asleep right away.

34
00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:25.259
I could feel all that water still inside me.

35
00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:29.200
The firefighters did not have enough water to put out the fire.

36
00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:30.593
But I did.

37
00:02:30.613 --> 00:02:31.834
"Stand back!"

38
00:02:32.374 --> 00:02:33.255
I shouted to them.

39
00:02:33.275 --> 00:02:35.016
"I will put out the fire.

40
00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:37.018
Please turn your backs to me and don't look."

41
00:02:38.479 --> 00:02:43.163
I did just what a little boy would do when he is outside and needs to go to

42
00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:43.823
the bathroom.

43
00:02:44.584 --> 00:02:46.666
I aimed through the open windows at the fire.

44
00:02:47.406 --> 00:02:49.308
Soon, the fire was out.

45
00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:54.492
"Hooray!" shouted the crowd of people who had been watching.

46
00:02:54.512 --> 00:02:57.514
"Three cheers for the Enormous One!

47
00:02:57.714 --> 00:02:59.336
He has saved the palace."

48
00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:03.699
The emergency was over, so I went back to my house.

49
00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.103
I was happy that I had been able to put out the fire.

50
00:03:08.864 --> 00:03:12.707
But I was worried that the king would not like the way I had done it.

51
00:03:13.588 --> 00:03:18.352
The king had a law about people doing what I had done right outside the palace.

52
00:03:19.433 --> 00:03:21.935
The next day, the king sent me a message.

53
00:03:22.616 --> 00:03:27.140
It said: Enormous One: Your behavior was against the law.

54
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.042
I realize, though, that there was no other way to put out the fire.

55
00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:36.625
So I will excuse your bad behavior just this once.

56
00:03:37.546 --> 00:03:40.027
I am grateful that you saved my palace.

57
00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.509
The queen was not as understanding as the king.

58
00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:45.830
My behavior disgusted her.

59
00:03:46.711 --> 00:03:51.233
She told everyone she would not allow the burned part of the palace to be repaired.

60
00:03:51.253 --> 00:03:55.396
"I will never go into those rooms again," she said.

61
00:03:56.285 --> 00:03:57.968
"I will never forgive the giant.

62
00:03:58.449 --> 00:03:59.912
He has no manners!"
